...
Let's try to mimic the zod validation by writing our own simple validator like this:
```
export default function App() {
const form = useForm({
validators: {
onChange: ({ value }) => {
return {
fields: {
...value.firstName.length < 3 && {
firstName: '[Custom] You must have a length of at least 3'
},
...!value.firstName.startsWith('A') && {
firstName: "[Custom] First name must start with 'A'"
},
...value.lastName.length < 3 && {
lastName: '[Custom] You must have a length of at least 3'
},
}
}
}
},
})
return (
//
)
}
```
Now the problem is gone.
All we ever did was remove the nested
```
message
```
property from the error map and return the error as string instead.

